# Quarto and reveal.js

British English; reproducible execution; cite at point of use.

## Markdown and cross-references

- Labels: `#fig-…`, `#tbl-…`, `#eq-…`, `{#sec-…}`; cite mid-sentence (`@fig-…`).
- Lists: standard Markdown only — no Pandoc example lists, task checkboxes, or
  unicode step markers (Visual Editor safe).
- Package names in backticks; citations `@key` unchanged.
- Callouts: `::: {#nte-… .callout-warning}` with `@nte-…` references.
- Emoji: `:shortcode:` with `from: markdown+emoji` when needed.

## Tables

- Manuscripts / static HTML: **`tinytable::tt()`** when the project uses it;
  otherwise repo convention.
- Slides / interactive HTML: **`reactable`** with `pagination = FALSE`,
  `echo: false` unless teaching code.

## Mermaid

Executable chunks:

````markdown
```{mermaid}
%%| label: fig-example
%%| fig-cap: "Caption."
flowchart TD
  A --> B
```
````

`eval: true` in site config or chunk. Inspect `pre.mermaid` + quarto-diagram JS
before client-side fallbacks.

## reveal.js slides

Read `~/.cursor/skills/quarto-revealjs/SKILL.md` (Slidecrafting) before major
deck edits. Official docs: https://quarto.org/docs/presentations/revealjs/

- One headline claim per slide; preview after edits (overflow is the main failure).
- Hierarchy: title → content → detail → attribution.
- `echo: false` by default; preserve citations when converting legacy decks.
- Optional: `quarto-revealjs-editable` in project `slides/` when already installed.
- Mermaid theme **sandstone** unless the deck defines otherwise.

## Slide design (dense decks)

| Element | Target size |
|---------|-------------|
| Diagram labels | 18–20px |
| Section headers | 14–16px |
| Body bullets | 12–13px |
| Metadata | 10–11px |

Below 10px: split the slide. Reuse backbone diagrams at section transitions.

Attribution plugin when configured: compact right-edge credits, not duplicate
HTML footers.
